The constructor is already minimal. It copies the base and four small members through the initializer list, so no meaningful speedup is available here. The time goes to `FieldBase`'s copy, and this function cannot change that.

The version below does the same thing with the same initialization order. The only difference is formatting, so you should expect no measurable speed change.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field),
      profile(field.profile),
      profileIndex(field.profileIndex),
      type(field.type),
      isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```